 {:name "tendsto-in-measure-ae-subsequence-api"
  :level :lemma-location
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Extract a strictly monotone subsequence converging almost everywhere from a sequence converging in measure."
   :lemma "`MeasureTheory.TendstoInMeasure.exists_seq_tendsto_ae`"
   :location
   "`Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.ConvergenceInMeasure`, in the `MeasureTheory` namespace"
   :statement-shape
   "From `TendstoInMeasure μ f atTop g`, obtain `∃ ns : ℕ → ℕ, StrictMono ns ∧ ∀ᵐ x ∂μ, Tendsto (fun i => f (ns i) x) atTop (𝓝 (g x))`."
   :use
   "First bridge the problem's convergence-in-measure definition to Mathlib's `TendstoInMeasure`; then invoke `.exists_seq_tendsto_ae` directly."
   :implementation-note
   "Mathlib's theorem already packages the fast `2⁻ᵏ` subsequence and first Borel-Cantelli argument, so callers should not rebuild that machinery unless their hypotheses cannot be converted to `TendstoInMeasure`."
   :boundary
   "The lemma consumes Mathlib's predicate, not an arbitrary problem-local strict-threshold definition; that conversion remains a separate obligation."}
